#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Three more encyclopedia pages from the 2026 scrape. No em-dashes."""
from page_lib import page, crumb, hero

page(
    "factions/sazanami.html",
    "The Sazanami clan",
    "Two centuries of Rakuzaichi: Kyora, Hakuri, the Tou, the Storehouse, and the auction that ended.",
    crumb(("Factions", "index.html"), "Sazanami")
    + hero("Auction house · 208 years", "The Sazanami clan", "漣", "A household that treated children as stock and called that civilization, until the discarded son inherited the building.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>The Sazanami are a criminal sorcerer clan who have run the Rakuzaichi, an annual black-market auction of artifacts, weapons, and people, for more than two hundred years. They are older than the Kamunabi. They are older than the Hishaku. They are not a government and not a conspiracy of ten. They are a firm. The 208th listing is Shinuchi. The eleventh head is <a href="../characters/kyora.html">Kyora</a>. The error that ends the firm is <a href="../characters/hakuri.html">Hakuri</a>. This page is the household the <a href="index.html">factions index</a> summarized in three paragraphs.</p>
      <p>Isou is the clan’s burial-force technique. The Storehouse (蔵, Kura) is the head’s subspace: loot, prisoners, weather as environmental control. In clan history, almost no one holds both. Hakuri does, once he stops scattering his own spirit energy. That dual inheritance is why the Kamunabi bother to keep Chihiro after the building falls. Bearers can be un-armed and re-armed without a siege. It is also why the Hishaku hunt Hakuri afterward. The auction was a building. Hakuri is the building that walks.</p>

      <h2>Kyora, eleventh head</h2>
      <p>Polite, absolute, father of a discarded son. He will sacrifice children to keep the Rakuzaichi on the calendar. When Chihiro corners him in the collapsing Storehouse, Kyora unsheathes Magatsumi and almost becomes someone else. He dies as himself, and uses the last of it to admit, too late, what he did to Hakuri. The Sword Master looks through an auctioneer’s eyes and still does not get a new bearer. Proxy is not contract. Full file: <a href="../characters/kyora.html">Kyora Sazanami</a>.</p>
      <p>Volume 3’s jacket puts him with Chihiro and Hiyuki: auction green-black against flame. Volume 5’s crowded jacket is Shinuchi heat. The title <em>Fervent</em> is the crowd. The man running the crowd is already dying into a masterpiece he listed but did not understand. Yura cracked the seal and left the ropes. Kyora thought he was selling a box. He was holding a person.</p>

      <h2>Hakuri</h2>
      <p>Disowned for perceived lack of ability. The inability was self-doubt: familial abuse scattered his spirit energy so Isou would not answer. When he chooses Chihiro, the architecture answers. He awakens Isou against Soya, then Storehouse, and becomes one of two Sazanami ever to hold both. He can register a person and their charged possessions and move Enchanted Blades across the country. He returns Tobimune to Samura at Senkutsuji. He is the reason Magatsumi can be hidden when Yukisada splits the HQ barrier. Full file: <a href="../characters/hakuri.html">Hakuri Sazanami</a>.</p>
      <p>Chihiro is the first person who treats the discarded son as a partner rather than defective inventory. That is the moral of the auction arc, under the architecture. The firm called children stock. The son became the warehouse. The 208th Rakuzaichi ends. The clan goes into hiding. Soya crawls out of rubble with amnesia, deduces he is Sazanami, and rediscovers a love of harming the weak. The extra packed with the tankōbon, <em>Soya Sazanami’s Memories, Begone!</em>, is a gag about memories he would like to misplace. It is not a redemption. See <a href="../fun/oneshots.html">volume extras</a>.</p>

      <h2>The Tou</h2>
      <p>The Tou (濤), Special Defense Corp, are the four best fighters in the clan. They follow the head and protect the auction.</p>
      <p><strong>Soya</strong>, older brother, heir apparent, obsessive about Hakuri, twisted affection as abuse. Once envious of Tenri’s superior sorcery, later fixated on the “untalented” brother. Demands Hakuri’s return, then resolves to kill him, then loses when Hakuri masters the house. Amnesia after the building falls. Still a Sazanami in the ways that matter to victims.</p>
      <p><strong>Tenri</strong>, younger brother, short blades, desperate to make Kyora proud. Uses a half-stable Datenseki tool against Chihiro. Jellyfish manifestation, then the pop. He dies of the lesson Part 2 is currently smelting in public: the mineral without Kunishige’s eyes is a crater. Sojo died of the same lesson at industrial scale.</p>
      <p><strong>Tamaki</strong>, older sister, one of the three who confront Chihiro and Shiba at the estate. Lies to Kyora that Soya is unwell; Tenri corrects her. <strong>Enji</strong>, older brother, begs Shiba for death after Tenri. Shiba tells him to live and raise what is left of the clan so another child does not eat a stone. That is Shiba’s ethics in one refusal. The Tou are not a raid team. They are a family military that dies of the father’s calendar.</p>

      <h2>The 208th</h2>
      <p>Shinuchi listed. Enten surrendered on purpose so the seventh blade can scout the Storehouse on its own charge. Mr. Inazuma (Yuu) wants his sister. Hiyuki arrives as the Kamunabi’s weapon. Yura walks the floor. Chihiro spends Cloud Gouger’s last charges to take Enten back. Prisoners leave. The Storehouse vanishes. Chihiro hands Magatsumi to the state and keeps Enten by joining them. Hakuri is the logistics in that deal. Full movement: <a href="../arcs/rakuzaichi.html">Rakuzaichi arc</a>. Locations: <a href="../world/locations.html">the Kura and the cemetery portal</a>.</p>
      <p>The Sazanami are not Hishaku. They sold a listing. They are not Kamunabi. They sold people. They are the book’s argument that an institution can be two centuries old and still be a crime the whole time. Hakuri is the argument that a child of that institution can still choose a different warehouse. Official chapters: VIZ / MANGA Plus.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="../characters/hakuri.html">Hakuri</a><a href="../characters/kyora.html">Kyora</a><a href="../arcs/rakuzaichi.html">Rakuzaichi</a><a href="hishaku.html">Hishaku</a><a href="kamunabi.html">Kamunabi</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "manga/publication.html",
    "Publication record",
    "Kagurabachi serialization, circulation, awards, English editions, and the 2027 anime, scraped current to August 2026.",
    crumb(("Manga Guide", "index.html"), "Publication")
    + hero("Jump 2023 #42 to now", "Publication record", "刊行", "From an ironic Big Three meme to four million copies, a Next Manga Award, and a Cypic series dated April 2027.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p><em>Kagurabachi</em> is written and illustrated by Takeru Hokazono. It began in <em>Weekly Shōnen Jump</em> issue 2023 #42, on 19 September 2023. Jump Comics Volume 1, <em>Mission</em>, landed 2 February 2024 (ISBN 978-4-08-883819-9). As of 1 May 2026 there are eleven Japanese tankōbon. Volume 12 is listed for 4 September 2026 (ISBN 978-4-08-885177-8). VIZ Media and MANGA Plus carry the English simulpub the same week as the magazine. VIZ’s first print volume arrived 5 November 2024 (ISBN 978-1-9747-4724-5). English Volume 9 is listed for 3 November 2026. Volumes 10 and 11 English are still TBD. This page is the circulation and awards desk. The <a href="volumes.html">volume guide</a> is the ISBN table. The <a href="chapters.html">chapter index</a> is the title list through 129.</p>

      <h2>How it landed</h2>
      <p>Promo art was a black coat, white type, and a fish. English Twitter decided it was the next Big Three before page one existed. Chapter 1 was the most-viewed new title on MANGA Plus in its first week. The series passed Spy × Family, Dragon Ball Super, and Boruto on that app’s popularity ranking. By April 2024 MANGA Plus had logged over 99 million page views. Ironic posts opened the chapter. The Vs. Sojo fight, Hakuri, and Samura are why people stayed. Hokazono was born in Osaka on 6 September 2000. The one-shot <em>Enten</em> placed at the 100th Tezuka Awards and ran in <em>Jump Giga</em> Spring 2021. Then Giga and Jump shorts: <em>Farewell! Cherry Boy!</em>, <em>Chain</em>, <em>Madogiwa de Amu</em>, <em>Roku no Meiyaku</em>. The serial is the first long work. Author file: <a href="../fun/hokazono.html">Hokazono</a>. Meme file: <a href="../fun/meme.html">meme to flagship</a>.</p>
      <p>Kōhei Horikoshi and Masashi Kishimoto have recommended the book. Vaundy has too. It ranked seventh on AnimeJapan’s 2024 Most Wanted Anime Adaptation poll. Da Vinci “Book of the Year”: 22nd in 2024, 13th in 2025. Sixth on Takarajimasha’s <em>Kono Manga ga Sugoi!</em> 2025 list for male readers. The 2023 joke is now a shelf that Circana BookScan and the New York Times graphic list have had to make room for, monthly, since late 2024.</p>

      <h2>Circulation</h2>
      <p>Shueisha’s restated numbers, because the meme predicted the opposite:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>July 2024: over 350,000 copies (including digital)</li>
        <li>August 2024: over 600,000</li>
        <li>October 2024: over 1 million</li>
        <li>December 2024: over 1.3 million</li>
        <li>May 2025: over 2.2 million</li>
        <li>October 2025: over 3 million sold</li>
        <li>April 2026: over 4 million in circulation</li>
      </ul>
      <p>North America: Circana BookScan monthly top 20 adult graphic novels since November 2024 (Volume 1 hit #1 that month). New York Times Graphic Books and Manga bestseller monthly list since December 2024. French edition via Kana, noted on Volume 11 promo. Other territories follow local Jump licenses. Buy the tankōbon. We do not list scans. <a href="../collectibles/index.html">Collectibles</a> is the shelf page.</p>

      <h2>Awards</h2>
      <p>2024: won the 10th Next Manga Award, print category. Nominated for the 70th Shogakukan Manga Award. 2025: nominated for the 49th Kodansha Manga Award (shōnen) and for the Eisner Award, Best U.S. Edition of International Material, Asia. 2026: won the Daruma for Best Action Manga at the Japan Expo Awards; nominated for Best Drawing and New Manga. Crunchyroll took seven Daruma at Japan Expo 2026’s 25th edition; Kagurabachi’s action win is the one this desk files. Nominations are not a personality. The Next Manga win is the one that matches the meme-to-flagship arc.</p>

      <h2>Anime</h2>
      <p>December 2024: Toyo Keizai reported Cypic (then CygamesPictures) via CyberAgent and Shochiku. April 2026: confirmed as a television series, Tetsuya Takeuchi directing, Keigo Sasaki on character designs, April 2027. First twenty minutes on a world tour from July 2026 (Anime Expo, Japan Expo, AnimagiC, Anime NYC), full first episode in Japan Q2 2027. Crunchyroll worldwide except Japan, mainland China, North Korea, South Korea. Muse Communication in South and Southeast Asia. Cast announced so far: Taihi Kimura (Chihiro; voiced comic: Shoya Ishige), Tomokazu Seki (Kunishige; voiced comic: Kenta Fujimaki), Katsuyuki Konishi (Shiba; voiced comic: Jun Fukushima). Hinao’s voiced-comic credit is Akari Tadano. More names will land closer to 2027. This page will not invent them. File: <a href="../media/anime.html">the anime</a>.</p>

      <h2>The magazine in 2026</h2>
      <p>Part 1 ends around chapter 115. Part 2 opens on 116. After 126, “Fire,” an announced rest. Return in August. Chapter 129, “Ironworks,” 23 August 2026. The chapter index and the <a href="part-2.html">forge desk</a> carry the uncollected titles. Volume 12 is expected to close the present-tense corridor and open the war book on paper. English editions trail Japanese dates by about nine months. Official week-to-week: <a href="https://www.viz.com/shonenjump/chapters/kagurabachi">VIZ Shonen Jump</a>, <a href="https://mangaplus.shueisha.co.jp/titles/100274">MANGA Plus</a> title 100274, <a href="https://www.shonenjump.com/j/rensai/kagurabachi.html">Weekly Shōnen Jump (JP)</a>. We do not host chapters, raws, or early Twitter dumps.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="volumes.html">Volumes</a><a href="chapters.html">Chapters</a><a href="part-2.html">Part 2</a><a href="../fun/hokazono.html">Hokazono</a><a href="../media/anime.html">Anime</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "guide/cast.html",
    "Who is who",
    "A compact Kagurabachi cast map: Chihiro’s circle, bearers, Kamunabi, Hishaku, Sazanami, and Part 2’s past.",
    crumb(("Guide", "index.html"), "Who is who")
    + hero("Start here · names", "Who is who", "人名案内", "The homepage stays small. This is the extra list of names the rows could not hold, with doors into the files.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>If you are sending the book to someone who only knows the hashtag, send <a href="../fun/first-read.html">first-read notes</a> and chapter 1 on MANGA Plus. If they have already finished Vs. Sojo and want names without a wiki spiral, this page is the map. Every name here already has a file, or lives on an org page until it earns one. Two Hishaku and two wartime blades stay unlabeled. This archive will not invent them.</p>

      <h2>The house</h2>
      <p><a href="../characters/chihiro.html">Chihiro Rokuhira</a>, 18, August 11, Enten, smith’s son, will not spend innocents. <a href="../characters/kunishige.html">Kunishige</a>, forged all seven, picky dealer, impossible eyes, murdered in the raid. <a href="../characters/chiaki.html">Chiaki Soga</a>, mother, Princess Soga, foresight, Part 2’s hope in the fire. <a href="../characters/akemura.html">Akemura Soga</a>, uncle, Sword Master, Magatsumi, Malediction. <a href="../characters/shiba.html">Togo Shiba</a>, teleport, family friend, left the bureau when the smith hid, Soga guardian in the past. Hinao runs Cafe Haru Haru. Char is the last Kyonagi, regeneration, Sojo’s stabilizer hunt.</p>

      <h2>Bearers</h2>
      <p><a href="../characters/samura.html">Seiichi Samura</a>, Tobimune, fastest, Iai, guilt as religion, dies holding Magatsumi back. <a href="../characters/iori.html">Iori</a>, daughter, memory-sealed, then not, inherits the support blade. <a href="../characters/uruha.html">Yoji Uruha</a>, Kumeyuri, prodigy, Crimson Recital when the contract is cut, loyal to the Rokuhira name. <a href="../characters/ibuki.html">Ibuki Misaka</a>, original Cloud Gouger, Samura’s equal, retired, killed by Hokuto. <a href="../characters/subaru.html">Subaru Urita</a>, sushi chef, surviving bearer, unnamed sword, duplication, helped start the project. Two wartime blades still have no printed names.</p>

      <h2>Kamunabi</h2>
      <p>Org file: <a href="../factions/kamunabi.html">Kamunabi</a>. <a href="../characters/kasen.html">Kasen</a>, director, leak. Ichiki, Yatsuru, seals. <a href="../characters/azami.html">Azami</a>, Coin, hid the smith. Izaru, beads, distrust. Kudo, Warrior’s Path, dies for Hakuri. <a href="../characters/hiyuki.html">Hiyuki</a>, Flame Bone. <a href="../characters/tafuku.html">Tafuku</a>, duel domain. <a href="../characters/natsuki.html">Natsuki Misaka</a>, Lightning Menace, Ibuki’s brother. <a href="../characters/kiri.html">Kiri Shirakai</a>, odachi, Iai’s granddaughter. Anti-Cloud Gouger: Hagiwara, Kugara, Kazane, Harima, Uzuki, Kasahara. Masumi: Ro, Moku, Sumi. Kokugoku Steam Squad, including Fushimi, die to Hiruhiko.</p>

      <h2>Hishaku</h2>
      <p>Org file: <a href="../factions/hishaku.html">Hishaku</a>. <a href="../characters/yura.html">Yura</a>, mind, raid, coin, body offered. <a href="../characters/hokuto.html">Hokuto</a>, puppet swordsman, killed Ibuki. <a href="../characters/hiruhiko.html">Hiruhiko</a>, Blood Crane, Play, eighteen. <a href="../characters/kuguri.html">Kuguri</a>, Twilight Wave, unrequited blade, Chihiro’s Iai dummy. Toto, blood tracking, fire-gate. Uran, ice, raid. Bingo, Mako, lion-dancer heads. Yukisada, 17, regeneration, HQ Vessel. Two unnamed.</p>

      <h2>Sazanami</h2>
      <p>Org file: <a href="../factions/sazanami.html">Sazanami</a>. Kyora, eleventh head. Hakuri, dual inheritance. Tou: Soya, Tenri, Tamaki, Enji. Two centuries of Rakuzaichi. The 208th ends the firm.</p>

      <h2>Part 2’s past</h2>
      <p>Magazine desk: <a href="../manga/part-2.html">Part 2</a>. Essay: <a href="../analysis/irishima.html">Irishima’s vein</a>. Hiroto and Yoshinojo Soga, killed later by Ariu Mikaboshi. Giyu, ambitious heir. Ariu, crown prince, Sumika. Hasumi, Datenseki lab. Mashiro, Shiba’s partner, Akuu, still alive in the talks. Joji, annoyed senior. The Mikaboshi as a people, not yet a theory about insects in Magatsumi. Kunishige has not yet looked at the stone. Enten does not exist. Chihiro has not been born.</p>
      <p>Voices announced for the 2027 Cypic series: Taihi Kimura (Chihiro), Tomokazu Seki (Kunishige), Katsuyuki Konishi (Shiba). Voiced comic: Shoya Ishige, Kenta Fujimaki, Jun Fukushima, Akari Tadano (Hinao). <a href="../media/anime.html">Anime page</a>. Technique names: <a href="../world/techniques.html">catalog</a>. Official chapters: VIZ / MANGA Plus.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="index.html">Guide</a><a href="../characters/index.html">Characters</a><a href="../factions/index.html">Factions</a><a href="../fun/first-read.html">First-read notes</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

